  "worked_solution": "Let's call $P(x)$ the given polynomial:\n\n$$\nP(x)={x}^{3}-4x\n$$\n\nThe degree $(n=3)$ is odd and the leading coefficient $({a}_{3}=1)$ is positive. Therefore, the polynomial has the following end behavior:\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nOnly the graph $A$ satisfies these conditions.",
